comments.body:
Ok thanks!
I guess that's the only lead we've got for now :/

Do you think you could apply this patch on top of master for your CI? Just to confirm..
```diff
diff --git a/src/mworker.c b/src/mworker.c
index a5ceff707..de905c882 100644
--- a/src/mworker.c
+++ b/src/mworker.c
@@ -485,6 +485,12 @@ void mworker_catch_sigterm(struct sig_handler *sh)
 	mworker_kill(sig);
 }
 
+void mworker_catch_sigint_test(struct sig_handler *sh)
+{
+	ha_warning("Exiting Worker process...\n");
+	exit(0);
+}
+
 /*
  * Performs some routines for the worker process, which has failed the reload,
  * updates the global load_status.
@@ -1283,6 +1289,7 @@ void mworker_apply_master_worker_mode(void)
 					close(child->ipc_fd[1]);
 			}
 		}
+		signal_register_fct(SIGINT, mworker_catch_sigint_test, SIGINT);
 		break;
 	default:
 		/* in parent */
```

@reporter that's it, vtest is still complaining about the exit status because it expects 0x82 (130) not 0, I should have included that in the test patch, ie: `exit(130)` instead of `exit(0)`:
```diff
diff --git a/src/mworker.c b/src/mworker.c
index a5ceff707..de905c882 100644
--- a/src/mworker.c
+++ b/src/mworker.c
@@ -485,6 +485,12 @@ void mworker_catch_sigterm(struct sig_handler *sh)
 	mworker_kill(sig);
 }
 
+void mworker_catch_sigint_test(struct sig_handler *sh)
+{
+	ha_warning("Exiting Worker process...\n");
+	exit(130); // make it looks like it was really interrupted by SIGINT
+}
+
 /*
  * Performs some routines for the worker process, which has failed the reload,
  * updates the global load_status.
@@ -1283,6 +1289,7 @@ void mworker_apply_master_worker_mode(void)
 					close(child->ipc_fd[1]);
 			}
 		}
+		signal_register_fct(SIGINT, mworker_catch_sigint_test, SIGINT);
 		break;
 	default:
 		/* in parent */
```

But clearly we see there that the test didn't last more than 2 seconds without activity and the worker exited when it wasn't the case before the patch
